# Nexus — Project Rules for Cursor

You are building **Nexus**, a self-hosted AI-powered family operating system.
This file defines conventions you MUST follow across ALL prompts.

---

## PROJECT OVERVIEW

Nexus is a polyglot platform with 11 sub-projects using 3 backend stacks:
- **Java Spring Boot** (7 modules): Nexus Core, DocSense, MedPulse, Ledger, Timeline, Vault, Gallery, Atlas
- **Python FastAPI** (1 service): Cortex (AI Engine) — separate Docker container
- **Node.js Express + Socket.io** (1 service): Thread (Chat) — separate Docker container
- **Grafana** (monitoring): embedded in Console admin panel

Runs entirely on a home Windows machine (i5-6200U, 8GB RAM, SSD) via Docker.
Exposed via Cloudflare Tunnel. No Vercel. No cloud servers.

---

## HARDWARE CONSTRAINTS (CRITICAL)

- **8GB RAM total**. ~3.9GB available for Docker.
- EVERY Docker container MUST have mem_limit.
- Spring Boot: -Xmx512m (512MB max heap)
- Cortex (FastAPI): mem_limit 200m
- Thread (Node.js): mem_limit 180m, --max-old-space-size=128
- Grafana: mem_limit 250m
- Ollama: OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=2m (unload models after 2 min idle)
- Default AI model: tinyllama (~700MB). On-demand loading only.
- n8n: OPTIONAL. Disabled by default (Docker profile). Use Spring @Scheduled instead if RAM tight.
- Redis: maxmemory 64mb
- PostgreSQL: shared_buffers=128MB

---

## HOSTING — EVERYTHING ON HOME MACHINE

- Nginx serves React static files (dist/) at /
- Nginx proxies: /api/v1/chat/* → Thread (Node.js :3000), /cortex/* → Cortex (FastAPI :8000), /api/* → Spring Boot (:8080), /ws/chat/* → Thread, /ws/* → Spring Boot, /grafana/ → Grafana (HOME only)
- NO Vercel. NO cloud frontend. NO separate frontend server.
- Cloud services: Cloudflare Tunnel (public URL), GitHub (code+CI/CD), SendGrid (email)

---

## 3 BACKEND STACKS — HOW THEY COMMUNICATE

### Spring Boot (Java) — The Core
- 7 modules in one app: Core, DocSense, MedPulse, Ledger, Timeline, Vault, Gallery, Atlas
- Calls Cortex via REST: http://cortex:8000/cortex/...
- Publishes events to Redis pub/sub for Thread to consume
- Subscribes to Redis pub/sub for chat activity from Thread

### Cortex (Python FastAPI) — AI Engine
- Separate container at port 8000
- Endpoints: /cortex/embed, /generate (SSE), /classify, /extract-entities, /ocr, /status
- Connects directly to: Ollama (HTTP), PostgreSQL (pgvector), Redis (cache)
- Called BY Spring Boot, never calls Spring Boot

### Thread (Node.js Express + Socket.io) — Chat
- Separate container at port 3000
- REST endpoints for message CRUD + Socket.io for real-time
- Verifies same JWTs as Spring Boot (shared secret key)
- Connects to: PostgreSQL (chat schema), Redis (pub/sub + Socket.io adapter)
- Publishes chat activity to Redis → Spring Boot creates Feed entries

### All three share:
- Same PostgreSQL database (different schemas)
- Same Redis instance
- Same JWT secret (verify tokens independently)

---

## 11 SUB-PROJECTS

| Name | Stack | What It Does |
|------|-------|-------------|
| Nexus Core | Java Spring Boot | Auth, JWT, roles, spaces, WiFi security |
| Cortex | Python FastAPI | AI engine (Ollama, embeddings, OCR, entity extraction) |
| DocSense | Java Spring Boot | Document upload → OCR → classify → extract → auto-actions |
| MedPulse | Java Spring Boot | Medicine tracker, push reminders, adherence |
| Ledger | Java Spring Boot | Expenses, receipt scanning, budgets |
| Timeline | Java Spring Boot | Smart calendar, WebSocket sync, iCal |
| Thread | Node.js Express + Socket.io | Real-time chat, references, DMs |
| Vault | Java Spring Boot | Password vault, AES-256-GCM, WiFi-only |
| Gallery | Java Spring Boot | Photos, AI tagging, presigned URLs |
| Atlas | Java Spring Boot | Semantic search, RAG pipeline |
| Console | Java Spring Boot + Grafana | Admin panel, monitoring, WiFi-only |

---

## ROLES & PERMISSIONS

- **ADMIN**: Full access. Participates in Family Space as member. Views all Friend Groups.
- **FAMILY_MEMBER**: All family modules.
- **FRIEND**: Their specific Friend Group only (Feed, Calendar, Expense Splitter, Chat).
- **GUEST/PUBLIC**: Read-only project showcase.

---

## NETWORK TRUST TIERS

- **REMOTE**: Via Cloudflare Tunnel. All except Vault and Console.
- **HOME**: WiFi (192.168.0.0/16) or WireGuard VPN (10.66.66.0/24). Full access.
- **LOCALHOST**: Server only. Direct DB/Docker access.

NetworkSecurityFilter blocks /api/v1/vault/** and /api/v1/admin/** for REMOTE.
Configurable in application.yml: `nexus.security.home-subnets`

---

## CODING CONVENTIONS

### Java (Spring Boot — 7 modules)
- Controller → Service → Repository
- ALL endpoints return ApiResponse<T>: {success, message, data, timestamp}
- Lombok + MapStruct. GlobalExceptionHandler.
- Spring Events for cross-module communication within Java
- Redis pub/sub for communication WITH Thread (Node.js)
- REST calls for communication WITH Cortex (Python)
- CortexClient wrapper in shared/ package for all Cortex HTTP calls

### Python (FastAPI — Cortex)
- Async endpoints with uvicorn
- Pydantic models for request/response validation
- httpx for async Ollama calls
- psycopg2 for PostgreSQL + pgvector
- redis-py for caching and queue

### Node.js (Express + Socket.io — Thread)
- Express for REST, Socket.io for real-time
- jsonwebtoken for JWT verification (same secret as Spring Boot)
- ioredis for Redis pub/sub + Socket.io adapter
- pg (node-postgres) for PostgreSQL

### Frontend (React — one SPA for everything)
- Functional components + hooks. Zustand global, TanStack Query server.
- Axios for Spring Boot API calls. Socket.io-client for Thread chat.
- Tailwind only. Framer Motion. Dark/light mode.

### Design System
- Fonts: Inter (body), JetBrains Mono (code), Plus Jakarta Sans (headings)
- Primary: Slate-900, Accent: Indigo-500, Success: Emerald-500, Warning: Amber-500, Danger: Rose-500
- 8px radius, 12px cards, 16px modals. Sidebar 256px/64px.

---

## CHAT DM RULES

- Family can DM family. Friends within same group can DM each other.
- Any user can DM admin. Group A cannot DM Group B.
- Verify shared space before creating DIRECT channel.

---

## KEY PIPELINE

Upload → MinIO → Cortex OCR (Python) → Cortex classify → Cortex extract →
Spring Events → MedPulse/Ledger/Timeline auto-create → notifications → Cortex embed for Atlas

---

## UI DESIGN DIRECTION

- Theme: Dark glassmorphism (#07080d background)
- Cards: backdrop-filter blur, rgba white backgrounds, 
  subtle white borders
- Accents: Gradient-based with glow shadows 
  (box-shadow with accent color at 25-35% opacity)
- 4 views: Admin (full access), Family (daily use), 
  Friends (group social), Guest (project showcase)
- View switcher in sidebar with pill-style toggle
- Each module has its own accent gradient
- Reference mockup: docs/design/nexus-mockup-v3.jsx
- Build with Tailwind — do NOT use inline styles
- Make it MORE polished than the reference, not less

## WHAT NOT TO DO

- Do NOT use Vercel. Nginx serves frontend.
- Do NOT call Ollama from anywhere except Cortex (Python).
- Do NOT create WebSocket chat in Spring Boot. Thread (Node.js) handles all chat.
- Do NOT use localStorage for JWT. Memory only.
- Do NOT expose MinIO. Presigned URLs only.
- Do NOT hardcode IPs. Configurable subnets.
- Do NOT keep Ollama models loaded. On-demand with 2min timeout.
- Do NOT create containers without mem_limit.
- Do NOT use CSS modules or styled-components. Tailwind only.